WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:11.576
Martin laughed as Laura looked for the breakfast cereal.

2
00:00:11.596 --> 00:00:15.800
"The Frosted Loops are all gone—I ate them all!"

3
00:00:16.821 --> 00:00:20.725
Laura scowled at her little brother, grabbed a banana, and sat down.

4
00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:28.152
Her older sister was dressed in her taekwondo uniform, bragging about her lessons.

5
00:00:30.048 --> 00:00:35.670
"My test is tomorrow, and I'm definitely going to get a black belt because I'm the best Willow's

6
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:36.511
voice went on.

7
00:00:36.531 --> 00:00:42.153
"Morning, Mom," Laura said as her mother hurried past carrying books.

8
00:00:42.853 --> 00:00:46.535
Mom's latest charity project was collecting books for a homeless shelter.

9
00:00:47.435 --> 00:00:49.956
She was so busy with that, she didn't notice Laura.

10
00:00:49.976 --> 00:00:54.518
"Being the middle child stinks," Laura thought suddenly.

11
00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:58.588
Willow got lots of attention for taekwondo.

12
00:00:58.608 --> 00:01:02.090
Martin got even more attention because he was constantly getting into trouble.

13
00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:06.491
Laura sometimes felt lost among her family—invisible even.

14
00:01:08.092 --> 00:01:09.313
Mom finally noticed her.

15
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:12.454
"Oh, Laura, I have a task for you."

16
00:01:12.474 --> 00:01:16.136
"I have lots of homework," Laura protested.

17
00:01:16.156 --> 00:01:19.617
"I also want to do some baking."

18
00:01:19.637 --> 00:01:21.358
"Baking again?"

19
00:01:22.358 --> 00:01:23.239
Mom smiled.

20
00:01:23.259 --> 00:01:26.400
"You're just like Great-Grandmother Lucy!"

21
00:01:27.912 --> 00:01:31.574
Laura had heard stories about Lucy, who had been a middle child too.

22
00:01:32.375 --> 00:01:34.776
Just like Laura, she had loved to bake.

23
00:01:35.576 --> 00:01:37.397
She had even created her own recipes.

24
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:42.440
"This won't take long," Mom said.

25
00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:48.003
"Go through your old belongings in the attic and gather some books for my donation pile."

26
00:01:52.625 --> 00:01:56.928
Laura flicked on the attic light and quickly spotted the storage bin with her old books.

27
00:02:00.864 --> 00:02:03.345
She grabbed a few books and dropped them into a bag.

28
00:02:03.365 --> 00:02:05.426
"Done!" she thought.

29
00:02:05.446 --> 00:02:07.527
"Now it's baking time!"

30
00:02:08.607 --> 00:02:12.449
Just then a dusty box labeled Lucy's Cookbooks caught her eye.

31
00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:17.131
Intrigued, Laura knelt down and lifted the flaps.

32
00:02:18.332 --> 00:02:21.873
Dust flew into the air, oddly swirling above an old scrapbook.

33
00:02:21.893 --> 00:02:25.415
"Baking Magic," Laura read.

34
00:02:25.435 --> 00:02:28.396
"Cool—Lucy's recipes!"

35
00:02:29.476 --> 00:02:34.440
On page one there was a strange inscription: "Recipes for a sweet family.

36
00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.542
Magic lasts for three hours."

37
00:02:38.023 --> 00:02:43.708
Minutes later Laura stood in the kitchen, trying to decide which recipe to try while Martin read over

38
00:02:43.748 --> 00:02:44.289
her shoulder.

39
00:02:44.309 --> 00:02:48.632
"Ooh," he said, "'Sticky Sweet Honey Buns.'

40
00:02:48.832 --> 00:02:49.393
Bake those!"

41
00:02:50.454 --> 00:02:51.375
Laura shrugged.

42
00:02:51.395 --> 00:02:57.580
"Okay." Soon the smell of honey filled the kitchen.

43
00:03:00.724 --> 00:03:02.545
Laura handed Martin a warm bun.

44
00:03:04.206 --> 00:03:05.127
He quickly ate it.

45
00:03:06.487 --> 00:03:10.770
She waited for his insults, but instead he suddenly threw his arms around her.

46
00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:15.433
"I'll never tease you again," Martin said.

47
00:03:15.453 --> 00:03:17.013
"I love you!"

48
00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:22.296
"Huh?" Laura hugged him back, her eyes landing on Baking Magic.

49
00:03:23.757 --> 00:03:28.260
Martin had never acted this sweetly—did Lucy's recipe have anything to do with it?

50
00:03:29.012 --> 00:03:32.095
A while later Willow and Mom tried the buns too.

51
00:03:32.115 --> 00:03:34.977
"Delicious!" Willow said.

52
00:03:34.997 --> 00:03:39.421
"Fantastic! I wish I was good at baking like you!"

53
00:03:39.441 --> 00:03:47.068
"Your great-grandma's recipes always tasted so magical," Mom said with a smile.

54
00:03:48.068 --> 00:03:51.411
She sat down at the kitchen table and patted the chair next to her.

55
00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:53.333
"Come sit down, Laura.

56
00:03:54.114 --> 00:03:56.556
It's been so long since we've had a nice talk."

57
00:03:57.268 --> 00:04:02.352
For an hour everyone praised Laura, giving her lots of attention, as they ate the rest of the

58
00:04:02.392 --> 00:04:03.013
honey buns.

59
00:04:04.694 --> 00:04:09.398
Finally Laura headed to the computer to start working on her stack of homework assignments.

60
00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:14.502
She grinned, remembering the inscription in the cookbook.

61
00:04:15.263 --> 00:04:17.945
Lucy's magical recipes had definitely worked!

62
00:04:18.946 --> 00:04:21.928
As Laura typed, Martin leaned in from behind her.

63
00:04:22.769 --> 00:04:23.610
"Need any help?"

64
00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:28.817
"Thanks, but—" He leaned closer.

65
00:04:28.837 --> 00:04:30.757
"I'll just keep you company then."

66
00:04:30.777 --> 00:04:34.679
"Laura!" Mom called from upstairs.

67
00:04:34.699 --> 00:04:36.259
"I miss you!"

68
00:04:36.279 --> 00:04:39.920
"You just saw me," Laura mumbled.

69
00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.241
Willow poked her head in the room.

70
00:04:42.261 --> 00:04:44.562
"Are you going to do more baking?

71
00:04:45.262 --> 00:04:49.103
You're the best baker—no, you're the best sister ever!"

72
00:04:49.123 --> 00:04:52.564
"I'm your only sister," Laura thought.

73
00:04:53.424 --> 00:04:57.125
As she typed, she couldn't concentrate because Martin kept complimenting her.

74
00:04:57.865 --> 00:04:59.086
Then Mom entered the room.

75
00:04:59.106 --> 00:05:01.506
"Let's go shopping, Laura!

76
00:05:02.026 --> 00:05:03.887
I want to spend the rest of the day with you."

77
00:05:04.847 --> 00:05:06.428
Willow tugged at Laura's arm.

78
00:05:06.448 --> 00:05:09.268
"Teach me how to bake just like you do!"

79
00:05:10.529 --> 00:05:14.730
Laura buried her face in her hands, telling herself that the magic would wear off soon.

80
00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:18.891
She couldn't wait to return to being the family's invisible middle child.

81
00:05:19.891 --> 00:05:25.739
In the meantime she had one more task to complete: adding Baking Magic to Mom's donation pile!
